\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For every bounded smooth simply connected planar domain and every nonzero first-positive Neumann Laplacian eigenfunction, including every vector in a multiple first eigenspace, is its gradient nonzero at every interior point and is every interior value strictly between its boundary minimum and maximum?

\subsection{Short English statement}
For every bounded smooth simply connected planar domain and every nonzero first-positive Neumann Laplacian eigenfunction, including every vector in a multiple first eigenspace, is its gradient nonzero at every interior point and is every interior value strictly between its boundary minimum and maximum?

